    "body": "A view of the Altar project area. Credit: Aldebaran Resources Inc.\nBy: Northern Miner Staff November 13, 2026\nDPM Metals (TSX: DPM; ASX: DPM) led the copper ranking with 1,054 metres grading 1.20% copper from 1,172 metres depth at Brevene Porphyry South in Bulgaria. Hole EX_BRESPO_03 included 465 metres at 1.44% copper and also topped the gold ranking on its gold grade.\nThe Sept. 20 results confirmed the discovery extends onto the adjoining Chelopech mine concession. DPM plans up to 15,000 metres of additional drilling from the concession by year-end to trace the system north and west and test how far it extends at depth.\nAldebaran Resources (TSXV: ALDE) placed second with a longer interval at a lower grade. Its Altar drilling in Argentina’s San Juan province returned 1,728.9 metres at 0.41% copper from 141 metres depth, including 756 metres at 0.61%. Copper Giant Resources (TSXV: CGNT) placed third at Mocoa in Colombia with 804 metres at 0.31% copper from 150 metres depth.\nThe chart ranks copper assays reported from Sept. 16 to Oct. 15, 2026, by grade multiplied by reported interval length. It shows the highest-scoring hole per property. Reported lengths may differ from true widths.\nPrint\nCOMMODITY: Copper\nCOMPANY: Aldebaran Resources Copper Giant Resources DPM Metals\nRepublish this article",
